## Context

Fifth slice of **ah-k6i**, the largest, on **ah-k6i.1** (planned; blocks this — `runReported`,
`failedStatus`, `warningStatus`). The path from a chosen file to a turn on screen lives in five
handlers of `AppShell.tsx` (`origin/main` `deb434a`, before .1): `applyReport` (:941-1036) — set
the report, commit it (`rememberTurn`, `gameMemory.ts:81`) unless a batch already did, read the
draft (`documentFor`, `orderDraft.ts:107`), build the status with counts, pick an opening hex if
nothing is selected; `storeReportOnly` (:1048-1084) — commit an older report for history without
touching the screen (gh-208); `loadReport` (:1086-1153) — flush, parse, `decideReportLoad`
(`reportLoadDecision.ts`), then ask / store-only / apply; `switchFaction` (:1156-1170) and
`mergeReport` (:1181-1220) — the two answers to the foreign-report prompt. Every decision that is
not already in `reportLoadDecision.ts` or `gameMemory.ts` sits inside the component: what a loaded
turn consists of, the prompt's snapshot of viewer and incoming, the older-turn message, the opening
selection. `restoreLatestTurn` (`gameMemory.ts:283-330`) already shows the shape: a plain function
that returns a `RestoredTurn` for the shell to apply in one place.

This bead moves the loading into `packages/shared/src/reportLoad.ts` — a `LoadedTurn` the shell
applies with **one** function — and collapses the five handlers to `runReported` calls. **One
player-visible change, chosen by the navigator (2026-08-15):** the report is shown only once its map
and orders came with it, so a commit or draft read that fails leaves the *previous* turn on screen
under the same red `could not read <file>: <error>` status — nothing half-applied (today the parsed
report is set first and stays up over an empty map when the second half fails). Everything else the
player sees is unchanged: strings, prompts, counts, busy.

## Files to change, and what to reuse

### New: `packages/shared/src/reportLoad.ts`

```ts
import type { CoreClient, MergedReportRecord, OpenedGame, ParsedReport, RememberedRegion } from "@atlantis/core-client";
import type { ImportStatus } from "./workspace/AppHeader";
import { commitTurn, rememberTurn, type MemoryOutcome } from "./gameMemory";
import { documentFor, draftKeyFor } from "./orderDraft";
import { decideReportLoad } from "./reportLoadDecision";
import { buildHexMapModel, unitsForHex } from "./hexMapModel";
import { warningStatus } from "./workspace/shellStatus";

/** Everything a turn brings to the screen, read before any of it is shown. */
export type LoadedTurn = {
  parsed: ParsedReport;
  rawReport: string;
  remembered: RememberedRegion[];
  merged: MergedReportRecord[];
  orders: string;
  ordersSavedAt: string | null;
  /** The counts, and the remember/draft warning if there was one - `applyReport`'s status (:996-1004). */
  status: ImportStatus;
};

/**
 * Reads everything a report needs to become the working turn: commits it (unless COMMITTED says a
 * batch already has - see `applyReport`'s note on why committing twice loses the ally's account),
 * reads back the map, and chooses saved orders over the report's template. No game: nothing is
 * remembered and the template is the document. Rejects when the commit or the read does; the
 * caller reports and applies nothing.
 */
export async function loadTurn(
  client: CoreClient, game: OpenedGame | null, report: ParsedReport, text: string,
  rulesetText: string | null, now: string, committed?: MemoryOutcome
): Promise<LoadedTurn>;

/** The hex and unit to land on when a turn opens into an empty selection (:1013-1022), or null. */
export function openingSelection(report: ParsedReport): { regionId: string; unitId: string | null } | null;

/** Commits an older report for history and says so; the screen is not touched (gh-208, :1048-1084). */
export async function storeOlderTurn(
  client: CoreClient, game: OpenedGame, report: ParsedReport, text: string, rulesetText: string | null,
  now: string, currentTurn: number
): Promise<ImportStatus>;   // warningStatus(warning ?? `turn ${n} stored for history; still showing turn ${currentTurn}.`)

/** Moved from AppShell.tsx:244-260 with its doc comment; exported because the shell holds one in state. */
export type PendingReportLoad = { … as today … };

export type ReportRoute =
  | { kind: "load" }
  | { kind: "storeOnly"; currentTurn: number }
  | { kind: "ask"; pending: PendingReportLoad };

/**
 * Where a parsed report goes: `decideReportLoad` plus the prompt's snapshot (:1105-1130) - the
 * viewer's identity is taken here, when the question is raised, never when it is answered.
 */
export function routeReport(
  viewer: ParsedReport | null, report: ParsedReport, text: string, fileName: string
): ReportRoute;

/** The parse the shell uses everywhere: classified when the ruleset is to hand, full otherwise (:1097-1100). */
export function reportParser(
  client: Pick<CoreClient, "parseReportClassified" | "parseReportFull">,
  ruleset: { status: "ready"; text: string } | { status: string }
): (text: string) => Promise<ParsedReport>;
```

`factionLabelOf` (:309-318) moves here too (`routeReport` needs it; export it — the shell uses it
for the header at :2407) with the `"an unnamed faction"` fallback applied exactly as at :1114/:1118.
`loadTurn` builds `status` as :996-1004 does (`regionCount: report.regions.length`, `unitCount`
summed, `message: memory.warning ?? chosen.warning`, `failed: false`, `warning: message !== null`).
Header doc: the ah-k6i story, `restoreLatestTurn` as the sibling shape, and the navigator's
"nothing half-applied" rule.

### `packages/shared/src/workspace/AppShell.tsx`

- Delete `PendingReportLoad` (:244-260, doc comment included) and `factionLabelOf` (:302-318); import from
  `../reportLoad`.
- **One applier**, beside the state it writes:
  ```ts
  /** Puts a loaded turn on screen - the only place a turn is applied, whichever way it arrived. */
  const applyLoadedTurn = useCallback((loaded: LoadedTurn) => {
    setParsed(loaded.parsed);
    setRawReport(loaded.rawReport);
    clearPlan();
    setRoute(null);
    setComparison(null);          // :959-963's comment moves here
    setTurnPickerOpen(false);
    setRemembered(loaded.remembered);
    setMergedReports(loaded.merged);
    setOrdersDocument(loaded.orders);
    setSave(savedStateFor(loaded.ordersSavedAt));
    setStatus(loaded.status);
    if (useWorkspaceStore.getState().selectedRegionId === null) {   // :1006-1022's comment moves here
      const opening = openingSelection(loaded.parsed);
      if (opening) selectRegion(opening.regionId, opening.unitId);
    }
  }, [clearPlan, selectRegion]);
  ```
- `applyReport(report, text, fileName, committed?)` becomes
  `runReported(async () => applyLoadedTurn(await loadTurn(client, game, report, text, rulesetText, new Date().toISOString(), committed)), (m) => setStatus(failedStatus(m)), { prefix: \`could not read ${fileName}\` })`
  — same deps minus `selectRegion`/`clearPlan` (now in `applyLoadedTurn`), plus it. Its doc comment
  (:930-940) stays, plus one line on the nothing-half-applied rule.
- `storeReportOnly(report, text, currentTurn)`: `if (!game) { setStatus(failedStatus("there is no open game to store it in")); return; } setStatus(await storeOlderTurn(client, game, report, text, rulesetText, now, currentTurn));` — it is only ever called inside `loadReport`'s `runReported`, so its rejection is reported there with the file name, as today's `catch` did.
- `loadReport(text, fileName)`:
  ```ts
  runReported(async () => {
    await flush();
    const report = await reportParser(client, ruleset)(text);
    const route = routeReport(parsed, report, text, fileName);
    if (route.kind === "ask") { setPendingOrdersImport(null); setPendingLoad(route.pending); return; }
    if (route.kind === "storeOnly") { await storeReportOnly(report, text, route.currentTurn); return; }
    await applyReport(report, text, fileName);
  }, (m) => setStatus(failedStatus(m)), { busy: setBusy, prefix: `could not read ${fileName}` })
  ```
  Keep the comments at :1090-1096 (why flush first, why classified) and :1108-1112 (why busy is
  released while the prompt is up — now `runReported`'s `finally`).
- `switchFaction`: `setPendingLoad(null); void runReported(() => applyReport(pending.report, pending.text, pending.fileName), () => {}, { busy: setBusy })` — hmm, no: `applyReport` already reports its own failure and never rejects; so simply `void (async () => { setBusy(true); try { await applyReport(...) } finally { setBusy(false) } })()` is what stays — **replace with** `void runReported(() => applyReport(pending.report, pending.text, pending.fileName), (m) => setStatus(failedStatus(m)), { busy: setBusy })` (the reporter is unreachable but honest).
- `mergeReport`: `setPendingLoad(null); void runReported(async () => { const outcome = await mergeTurn(client, game, pending.viewer.factionId, pending.viewer.turnNumber as number, pending.text, rulesetText, now); setRemembered(outcome.remembered); setMergedReports(outcome.merged); setStatus({ regionCount: outcome.result.mergedRegionCount, unitCount: 0, message: describeMerge(outcome.result), failed: false, warning: false }); }, (m) => setStatus(failedStatus(m)), { busy: setBusy, prefix: \`could not merge ${pending.fileName}\` })` — its doc comment (:1172-1180, "that temptation is the bug") stays word for word.
- The four `parseReportClassified`/`parseReportFull` choices at :1097-1100, :1460-1463 (batch —
  ah-k6i.6 will use `reportParser`; leave that one), :1615-1618 (restore effect: use
  `reportParser(client, ruleset)` here too — one line), :2467-2470 (comparison — .3 may have
  rewritten it; use `reportParser` if that code is still here, otherwise leave .3's).
- The restore effect (:1596-1660) **keeps** its own apply sequence — it applies a `RestoredTurn`,
  which has no `status` counts; do not force it through `applyLoadedTurn` here (say so in a comment
  by `applyLoadedTurn`: the restore is the one other place a turn reaches the screen, and it is an
  effect with cancellation).

### Tests

New `packages/shared/src/reportLoad.test.ts` (plain-module style; fakes as object literals of
`vi.fn()`; a `ParsedReport` fixture built inline as `gameMemory.test.ts` does — look there first):

- `loadTurn`: with a game, calls `rememberTurn`'s client methods (stub the client the way
  `gameMemory.test.ts` stubs `commitTurn`/`rememberTurn` — or spy on `rememberTurn` via
  `vi.mock("./gameMemory")`; pick the file's own existing pattern) and `documentFor`; returns
  `orders` from the saved draft when there is one, the template when not; `status` counts regions
  and units, `warning: true` iff a warning came back, `message` = the remember warning first, else
  the draft warning; with `committed` given, does **not** remember again; without a game: empty
  `remembered`/`merged`, template orders, `warning: false`. A rejecting remember rejects `loadTurn`.
- `openingSelection`: a report whose first own-unit hex is not the first region → that hex and its
  first unit; a report with no units → the initial region with `unitId: null`; keep it to what
  `buildHexMapModel`'s `initialSelectedRegionId` gives.
- `storeOlderTurn`: returns `warningStatus("turn 70 stored for history; still showing turn 71.")`
  when the commit had no warning, and the commit's warning when it had one.
- `routeReport`: viewer null → `load`; same faction newer turn → `load`; older turn → `storeOnly`
  with `currentTurn`; other faction same turn → `ask` with `canMerge: true` and the exact snapshot
  (`viewer.factionLabel` from the viewer report, `"an unnamed faction"` when it has none); other
  faction different turn → `ask` with `canMerge: false`. Mirror `reportLoadDecision.test.ts`'s
  fixtures.
- `reportParser`: `ready` → `parseReportClassified(text, rulesetText)`; anything else →
  `parseReportFull(text)`.

## Increments

1. RED: `routeReport`, `reportParser`, `factionLabelOf` cases. GREEN: those three (moving the type
   and `factionLabelOf`); the shell imports them (typecheck).
2. RED: `loadTurn`, `openingSelection`, `storeOlderTurn`. GREEN: the module.
3. `applyLoadedTurn` and the five handler rewrites; the restore effect's parser line; typecheck; the
   shared suite; then the full gate.
4. PR `refactor(ah-k6i.5): loading a report is reportLoad.ts, applied by the shell in one place`,
   `@copilot`, CI, squash. Close the bead, not the epic (ah-k6i.6 remains, and it builds on this).

## The test plan

- Unit: `reportLoad.test.ts` (new), `reportLoadDecision.test.ts`, `gameMemory.test.ts`,
  `orderDraft.test.ts`, `shellAction.test.ts`, whole shared suite.
- `pnpm run check`; the smoke suite imports reports, answers the foreign-report prompt both ways and
  checks the status counts (`tests/smoke/workspace.spec.ts` — `grep -n "Switch faction\|Merge\|regions"`).

## User-facing decisions

Navigator (2026-08-15): **nothing half-applied** — a report is shown only with its map and orders;
a failed commit/draft read leaves the previous turn on screen under `could not read <file>: <error>`
(rejected: keep today's two-step apply, where the new report stays up over an empty map after such
a failure — more surface for the same information). All strings unchanged and quoted above.

## Out of scope

- The batch import (`importReports`, `runBatch`, `chooseOrdersImport`) — ah-k6i.6, which will call
  `loadTurn`/`applyLoadedTurn` and `reportParser`.
- Routing the restore effect through `applyLoadedTurn`.
- Any change to `ForeignReportPrompt`, `reportLoadDecision.ts`, `gameMemory.ts`, `orderDraft.ts`.

## Validation

```bash
pnpm --filter @atlantis/shared test -- reportLoad reportLoadDecision gameMemory orderDraft shellAction
pnpm --filter @atlantis/shared typecheck && pnpm --filter @atlantis/shared lint
pnpm run check
```

Human check (Psylocke): open a report into an empty game (counts on the status line, opening hex
selected); open a newer turn of the same faction (draft preferred over template if one was saved);
open an older turn (status says stored for history, screen unchanged); open an ally's report for the
same turn and Merge, then another and Switch faction. All as before.

## Known traps

- **`applyReport`'s `committed` argument is load-bearing** for the batch (ah-k6i.6, and today's
  `runBatch` at :1287-1416 calls `applyReport(..., committed)`): keep the parameter and the comment
  at :944-953 — a second commit would drop the ally's account of shared hexes.
- **The opening selection reads the store synchronously** (`useWorkspaceStore.getState()` at
  :1013) — keep it in the shell's applier; the module only computes the candidate.
- **`storeReportOnly` reports through the enclosing `runReported`** — do not give it its own
  try/catch again; today's message for its failure is `could not read <file>: …` from `loadReport`'s
  catch, and the prefix keeps that.
- **`mergeReport`'s status carries a count** — it is not `warningStatus`/`failedStatus`; leave the
  literal.
- **No DOM renderer**; every assertion goes in the module. **`pnpm run check`'s tooling worktree
  test** may fail on scratch worktrees (ah-efj); finish the gate by hand and say so.
- `AppShell.tsx` shifts under every merged sibling (.2-.4); re-grep everything above when branching.

## Context

Third slice of **ah-k6i**, on **ah-k6i.1** (planned; blocks this — `runReported`, `describeError`,
`warningStatus` in `packages/shared/src/workspace/shellAction.ts` / `shellStatus.ts`; read its plan,
and note it already rewrites `handleOpenTurnPicker` to run through `runReported` — this bead moves
what .1 left inline into a module). Two handlers in `AppShell.tsx` (`origin/main` `deb434a`, before
.1) own the turn picker and the comparison: `handleOpenTurnPicker` (:2412-2423) — list the game's
imported turns and keep the viewer's faction's; and `handleSelectComparisonTurn` (:2441-2497) —
guard, decide via `toggleComparison` (`turnCompare.ts:27-39`) whether the click starts, switches or
stops a comparison, load and parse the turn through `loadComparisonTurn` (`AppShell.tsx:229-243`,
already extracted, still living in the component file with its tests in `AppShell.test.ts:126-181`),
and put a warning on the status line when the load fails (ah-6l2, the P0 that started all this).

This bead moves the doing into one plain module beside `turnCompare.ts`, moves `loadComparisonTurn`
and its tests with it, and leaves the shell two `runReported` calls. **No player-visible change**:
the same warnings, the same picker close rules.

## Files to change, and what to reuse

### New: `packages/shared/src/comparisonActions.ts`

```ts
import type { CoreClient, ImportedTurnSummary, ParsedReport } from "@atlantis/core-client";
import { toggleComparison, type ComparisonTurn } from "./turnCompare";

export type ComparisonClient = {
  listImportedTurns: CoreClient["listImportedTurns"];
  loadImportedTurn: CoreClient["loadImportedTurn"];
};

/** The turns the picker offers: the game's imported turns, this faction's only, as the client orders them. */
export async function listComparableTurns(
  client: Pick<ComparisonClient, "listImportedTurns">, databasePath: string, gameId: string, factionId: string
): Promise<ImportedTurnSummary[]>;

/** Moved verbatim from AppShell.tsx:221-243, doc comment included. */
export async function loadComparisonTurn(
  client: Pick<ComparisonClient, "loadImportedTurn">, databasePath: string, gameId: string,
  factionId: string, turnNumber: number, parse: (rawReport: string) => Promise<ParsedReport>
): Promise<ComparisonTurn>;

/** Where the working turn stands when a turn is clicked; `working` null means no report is on screen. */
export type ComparisonContext = {
  databasePath: string;
  gameId: string;
  factionId: string;
  workingTurn: number;
  currentTurn: number | null;
  parse: (rawReport: string) => Promise<ParsedReport>;
};

/**
 * What a click on CLICKED-TURN in the picker does to the comparison.
 * `{ changed: false }`: nothing (the working turn, or the turn already compared, was clicked) - the
 * picker just closes. `{ changed: true, comparison: null }`: stop comparing.
 * `{ changed: true, comparison }`: compare against the loaded turn. Rejects (through
 * `loadComparisonTurn`) when the turn will not load, with an Error the caller reports.
 */
export async function pickComparisonTurn(
  client: Pick<ComparisonClient, "loadImportedTurn">, context: ComparisonContext, clickedTurn: number
): Promise<{ changed: false } | { changed: true; comparison: ComparisonTurn | null }>;
```

`pickComparisonTurn` body: `const next = toggleComparison(context.currentTurn, clickedTurn,
context.workingTurn); if (next === context.currentTurn) return { changed: false }; if (next === null)
return { changed: true, comparison: null }; return { changed: true, comparison: await
loadComparisonTurn(client, context.databasePath, context.gameId, context.factionId, next,
context.parse) };` — note `next === clickedTurn` on the load path, so the caller's prefix can name
`clickedTurn`. Header doc: the ah-6l2 rule — every exit either changes the comparison or rejects,
never "nothing happened silently" — carried over from `handleSelectComparisonTurn`'s comment
(:2424-2440), which moves here.

### `packages/shared/src/workspace/AppShell.tsx`

- Delete `loadComparisonTurn` (:221-243) and import it — actually import only what the shell now
  uses: `listComparableTurns`, `pickComparisonTurn` from `../comparisonActions`.
- `handleOpenTurnPicker` (after .1):
  ```ts
  const summaries = await runReported(
    () => listComparableTurns(client, game.databasePath, gameId, factionId),
    (message) => { setStatus(warningStatus(message)); setTurnPickerOpen(false); },
    { prefix: "could not list the turns to compare" }
  );
  if (summaries !== undefined) setTurnSummaries(summaries);
  ```
- `handleSelectComparisonTurn(clickedTurn)`:
  ```ts
  const workingTurn = parsed?.header.turnNumber ?? null;
  const reportComparisonFailure = (message: string) => { setStatus(warningStatus(message)); setTurnPickerOpen(false); };
  if (workingTurn === null || !game || !parsed?.header.factionId) {
    reportComparisonFailure(`could not load turn ${clickedTurn} for comparison`);   // :2447-2451, unchanged text
    return;
  }
  const parse = (text: string) => ruleset.status === "ready" ? client.parseReportClassified(text, ruleset.text) : client.parseReportFull(text);
  await runReported(
    async () => {
      const pick = await pickComparisonTurn(client, { databasePath: game.databasePath, gameId: game.manifest.metadata.gameId, factionId: parsed.header.factionId, workingTurn, currentTurn: comparison?.key.turnNumber ?? null, parse }, clickedTurn);
      if (pick.changed) setComparison(pick.comparison);
      setTurnPickerOpen(false);
    },
    reportComparisonFailure,
    { prefix: `could not load turn ${clickedTurn} for comparison` }
  );
  ```
  Same deps as today (`[client, comparison, game, parsed, ruleset]`). The doc comment keeps its two
  rules (never `setParsed`; a failure is a `warning`, not `failed`, and why — :2427-2440), minus the
  paragraph that moved to the module. The `void` call sites at :2721 and :2728 are unchanged.

### `packages/shared/src/workspace/AppShell.test.ts` → `packages/shared/src/comparisonActions.test.ts`

- Move the `loadComparisonTurn` describe block (:126-181) verbatim, importing from
  `../comparisonActions` (drop `loadComparisonTurn` from `AppShell.test.ts`'s import).
- Add: `listComparableTurns` filters to the faction and keeps order (a fake client returning three
  summaries for two factions). `pickComparisonTurn`: clicking the working turn → `{ changed: false
  }` and no client call; clicking the compared turn → `{ changed: true, comparison: null }`; another
  turn → loads it (fake `loadImportedTurn` + `parse`) and returns it; a turn that will not load
  rejects with the `Error` from `loadComparisonTurn` (matching `/70/`).

